   "definition_quote": "There are $N$ arms. At time $t = 1, 2, \\ldots $, a context vector $b_i(t) \\in {\\mathbb R}^d$, is revealed for every arm $i$. These context vectors are chosen by an adversary in an adaptive manner after observing the arms played and their rewards up to time $t-1$... We assume that $\\eta_{i,t}=r_i(t)-b_i(t)^T\\mu$ is conditionally $R$-sub-Gaussian... We will also assume that $||b_i(t)||\\le 1$, $||\\mu||\\le 1$, and $\\Delta_i(t) \\le 1$"
  }
